---
layout: base.njk
title: "NaturalTag™"
summary: "NaturalTag™ is a food-grade, in-product authentication tag made from inactivated probiotics, incorporated directly into products during manufacturing."
permalink: /naturaltag/
---

{# The product mark, blended into the hero rather than sitting in a panel.
   Kirsty asked for the product icons to be somewhere on the page once the
   hero panel became a photograph. Same technique as the call-to-action
   watermark: the icon is a mask, so the colour comes from the stylesheet
   and the mark sits tonally on this page's own tint instead of being
   stamped on it in whatever colour the file happens to be.

   The class only appears when a mark is set, so clearing the field in the
   panel removes it. The url filter is required: HtmlBasePlugin does not
   look inside a style attribute. #}
<section class="challenge hero-tag{% if naturaltag.hero_mark %} solution-hero-mark{% endif %}"
  style="padding-top:9rem{% if naturaltag.hero_mark %};--hero-mark:url('{{ naturaltag.hero_mark | url }}'){% endif %}">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="challenge-grid">
      <div class="challenge-text">
        <span class="section-label">{{ naturaltag.label }}</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">{{ naturaltag.title }}</h2>
        <p class="section-subtitle">{{ naturaltag.hero }}</p>
        <p class="challenge-lead" style="margin-top:1.5rem">{{ naturaltag.intro }}</p>
        <a href="{{ naturaltag.cta_url }}" class="btn btn-primary" style="cursor:pointer">{{ naturaltag.cta_text }}</a>
      </div>
      {# A photograph if there is one, the logo panel if not. NaturalCloud is
         still on the panel: its imagery is a video Kirsty is having made, and
         a stand-in photograph would be worse than the mark. #}
      {% if naturaltag.hero_image %}
      <div class="solution-photo">
        {# object-position lets an editor move the crop without a new file.
           The NaturalTag photograph is 3:2 and this panel is 4:3, so 12% of the
           width is cropped; centred, that put the vial at 41% across. #}
        <img src="{{ naturaltag.hero_image }}" alt="{{ naturaltag.hero_image_alt }}" loading="lazy"{% if naturaltag.hero_image_position %} style="object-position:{{ naturaltag.hero_image_position }}"{% endif %}>
      </div>
      {% else %}
      <div class="solution-mark">
        <img src="{{ naturaltag.hero_logo }}" alt="{{ naturaltag.hero_logo_alt }}" loading="lazy">
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="valueprop">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="vp-grid about-grid-2">
      <article class="vp-card">
        <h3>{{ naturaltag.why_title }}</h3>
        <ul class="sol-list" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;margin-top:0">
          {% for item in naturaltag.why_items %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="vp-card">
        <h3>{{ naturaltag.features_title }}</h3>
        <ul class="sol-list" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;margin-top:0">
          {% for item in naturaltag.features %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- How It Works, back on this page from 12 Aug, alongside the copy on the
    homepage rather than instead of it. Both render from partials/how-it-works
    and both read _data/home.yml, so there is one set of words and two places
    it appears.

    It left this page on 8 Aug when Kirsty said Section 4 was missing from the
    homepage. What nobody noticed was that the homepage's own "See how it
    works" link still pointed at /naturaltag/#how-it-works, an anchor that had
    gone with it, so for four days that link landed at the top of this page and
    left the reader to find the section themselves. The healthcheck now
    resolves fragments as well as paths. -#}
{% include "partials/how-it-works.njk" %}

<section class="howitworks">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="how-head">
      {# The label used to print matrices_title, so the eyebrow and the heading
         said two unrelated things. #}
      <span class="section-label">{{ naturaltag.matrices_label }}</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">{{ naturaltag.video_title }}</h2>
      <p  style="color:rgba(255,255,255,.65);font-size:.98rem;line-height:1.8">{{ naturaltag.video_description }}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="how-grid how-grid-3">
      {% for m in naturaltag.matrices %}
      <div class="how-step">
        <h3>{{ m.group }}</h3>
        <p>{{ m.items }}</p>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div  style="margin-top:3.5rem;border-radius:20px;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:var(--shadow-lg)">
      <video src="{{ naturaltag.video_src }}" muted loop playsinline autoplay style="width:100%;display:block"></video>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="finalcta">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="finalcta-inner">
      <h2>Your product's identity starts at the source.</h2>
      <div class="finalcta-actions">
        <a href="{{ naturaltag.cta_url }}" class="btn btn-white" style="cursor:pointer">{{ naturaltag.cta_text }}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
